# This file is used to set environment variables for the application.
# You can change the values of these variables to configure the application.
# The application will use these variables to determine its behavior.
# You can set the following variables (add or remove # as needed):
#
# HTTPS configuration
HTTPS=true
#
# API Configuration
# REACT_APP_API_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# Important Notes:
#
# Example for accessing the API URL in the code:
# const apiUrl = process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL;
#
# Prefix Requirement: In Create React App (which you're using via react-scripts), environment variables must be prefixed with REACT_APP_ to be accessible in your frontend code.
# 
# No Dynamic Updates: Environment variables are embedded during build time. If you change them, you need to restart your development server.
# 
# Public Information Only: Remember that all environment variables in your frontend are publicly visible to users. Never store secrets like API keys there.
# 
# Loading Order: Environment variables are loaded in this priority:
# .env.development.local or .env.production.local (highest priority)
# .env.development or .env.production
# .env.local
# .env (lowest priority)